*Heading
 Net pull-out, ALTERNATED weave -- JOB 1/5 of a restart chain: Phase A (ENGAGE) -- quadratic C3D10M, alpha=1000 damping (beta=0)
** ==========================================================================
** This is job 1 of 5 in a chain where EACH dismech phase is its own
** Abaqus job, writing its OWN .odb, linked by *Restart:
**
**   job (this file)              writes            restart-reads from
**   net_pullout_phaseA_engage     .odb/.res          (fresh model)
**   net_pullout_phaseB_hold       .odb/.res          oldjob=net_pullout_phaseA_engage
**   net_pullout_phaseC_release    .odb/.res          oldjob=net_pullout_phaseB_hold
**   net_pullout_phaseD_free       .odb/.res          oldjob=net_pullout_phaseC_release
**   net_pullout_phaseE_pullout    .odb/.res          oldjob=net_pullout_phaseD_free
**
** WHY: a crash/kill during a LATER phase (most likely PULLOUT: the
** longest step, 1.2 s, with the largest sliding motion) must not put the
** EARLIER phases' results at risk. Splitting into 5 jobs means each
** completed phase's .odb is a closed, independent file on disk the
** moment that job exits 0 -- nothing a later job does can touch it.
** Run the chain with run_phaseA_to_E_chained.sh, which stops immediately
** if any job fails (so you never restart a later phase from a dead one).
**
** SECOND LAYER: even within ONE job, *Restart, write below fires several
** times per step (not just once at the end), so a crash partway through
** a long step (e.g. PULLOUT, job 5) can be resumed from the last
** checkpoint instead of redoing the whole step -- see job 5's own
** header for the oldjob=itself / step=1 recipe. NOTE: this specific
** job (A/ENGAGE) does NOT support that in-place resume as written --
** it has no *Restart, read card (it is the fresh-model starting job),
** so RESUME_INPLACE on job A would just rerun ENGAGE from t=0, not
** resume mid-step. If Phase A itself ever needs this, add
** "*Restart, read, step=1" right before "*Step, name=ENGAGE" below.
**
** All phase-mapping, timing and physics comments from the single-job
** version (net_pullout_phaseA_to_E_explicit.inp) apply unchanged; see
** that file for the full dismech-to-Abaqus phase correspondence table.
** This job carries the complete model (mesh, material, contact,
** permanent BCs, both amplitudes); jobs 2-5 are thin restart
** continuations that each add only their own step.
** ==========================================================================
** THIS VARIANT (see ./README.md): quadratic tetrahedra (C3D10M) instead
** of linear C3D4 (see ../quadratic_C3D10M_nodamping/README.md for the
** undamped baseline), with pure mass-proportional Rayleigh damping
** added: *Damping, alpha=1000, beta=0. This deck is one point of a
** damping-coefficient sweep (alpha = 1, 10, 50, 100, 1000 s^-1)
** characterizing the Rayleigh coefficient needed before damping
** measurably affects the model's response; see ../quadratic_C3D10M_
** alpha1000/README.md for the energy-based derivation (comparing
** ALLVD against ALLIE) behind the value used in the paper. Beta is
** left at zero because stiffness-proportional damping further reduces
** the explicit stable timestep, which mass-proportional damping at
** these magnitudes does not.
**
** At alpha<=1000, zeta = alpha/(2*omega) stays below ~4e-4 even at the
** mesh's own stability-limiting frequency (~1.33e6 rad/s), so damping
** does not interact with the mass-scaling target below; dt stays at
** the baseline value, 1.5e-6. Contact, BCs, step timings, amplitudes
** and output requests are otherwise identical to the archived linear
** baseline.
** ==========================================================================
*Preprint, echo=NO, model=NO, history=NO, contact=NO
**
